ticle-title>Polygenic influence on plasma homocysteine: association of two prevalent mutations, the 844ins68 of cystathionine beta-synthase and A(2756)G of methionine synthase, with lowered plasma homocysteine levels</article-title><source>Atherosclerosis</source><year>2000</year><volume>149</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>137</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Atherosclerosis||149|131||bib21|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10704624</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Uchida</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayashi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawakami</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Schneider</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Yochim</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuramochi</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Takasaki</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Danenberg</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name><name><surname>Danenberg</surname><given-names>PV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Loss of heterozygosity at the thymidylate synthase (TS) locus on chromosome 18 affects tumor response and survival in individuals heterozygous for a 28-bp polymorphism in the TS gene</article-title><source>Clin Cancer Res</source><year>2004</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>433</fpage><lpage>439</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Clin Cancer Res||10|433||bib22|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14760062</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Villafranca</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Okruzhnov</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Dominguez</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Garcia-Foncillas</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name>